=== [Iter 0015] 2026-09-16 13:00:27 | Category: Technical ===
Question: "how does fold-local median imputation prevent future data leakage" (Context: Bidong, Tab: overview)
Response (2.35s) | Title: Data Integrity: Fold-Local Median Imputation | Pose: answer | Links: 2
  [MECHANISM]: Fold-local median imputation ensures that missing values in the Reef Check Malaysia dataset are filled using only the statistics derived from the training fold. By calculating the median exclusively within the temporal or spatial subset defined by the cross-validation split, the model prevents information from the validation or test sets from influencing the training process.
  [LEAKAGE PREVENTION]: 1. Temporal Isolation: Prevents future-dated observations from biasing current-year predictions.
2. Spatial Independence: Ensures monitoring units with missing data do not inherit global trends that would artificially inflate performance metrics.
3. Statistical Integrity: Maintains the independence of the 95% pooled forward-test residual distribution [-16.25, +13.66 pp/yr].
  [MODEL CONTEXT]: This imputation strategy supports the Gradient Boosting Regressor, which achieves a MAE of 5.862 pp/yr. It is a critical component of the ReefSafe pipeline to ensure that the 404 monitoring-unit rows remain robust for ecological screening.
  [LINKS]: Reef Check Malaysia annual reports, OpenDOSM Data Catalogue

