=== [Iter 0068] 2026-09-16 13:05:48 | Category: Technical ===
Question: "how does fold-local median imputation prevent future data leakage" (Context: Lang Tengah, Tab: overview)
Response (3.02s) | Title: Data Integrity: Fold-Local Median Imputation | Pose: answer | Links: 2
  [METHODOLOGY]: To prevent data leakage, ReefSafe employs fold-local median imputation within our cross-validation pipeline. Instead of calculating the global median across the entire 2007-2025 dataset, the model computes the median exclusively from the training fold. This ensures that information from the validation or test sets remains unseen during the training phase.
  [LEAKAGE PREVENTION]: 1. Isolation: Training folds are treated as independent temporal subsets.
2. Temporal Integrity: By restricting imputation to training-fold statistics, we prevent the model from 'peeking' at future trends or mean values that would otherwise bias the Gradient Boosting Regressor.
3. Consistency: This approach maintains the statistical distribution of the 404 monitoring units while preserving the validity of our 5.862 pp/yr MAE performance metric.
  [LINKS]: Reef Check Malaysia annual reports, OpenDOSM Data Catalogue

