=== [Iter 0083] 2026-09-16 13:07:16 | Category: Technical ===
Question: "how does fold-local median imputation prevent future data leakage" (Context: Lima, Tab: overview)
Response (2.36s) | Title: Data Integrity: Fold-Local Median Imputation | Pose: answer | Links: 0
  [METHODOLOGY]: To prevent data leakage in the ReefSafe Gradient Boosting Regressor, we employ fold-local median imputation. This ensures that missing values in a specific cross-validation fold are filled using only the median statistics calculated from the training subset of that same fold. By excluding the validation set from the imputation calculation, we prevent information from the future (or unseen data) from influencing the training process.
  [LEAKAGE PREVENTION]: 1. Isolation: Imputation parameters are derived strictly from training-fold observations.
2. Temporal Integrity: Prevents the model from 'seeing' the global distribution of the target variable across the entire time-series.
3. Bias Mitigation: Ensures that the MAE of 5.862 pp/yr reflects true predictive performance on unseen monitoring units.

