  [DEFINITION]: The Reef-Adjacent Economy represents the annual visitor spending proxy attributed to marine park tourism. It is calculated as 1,464,770 annual visitors multiplied by the RM410 average expenditure per visitor (DOSM Domestic Tourism Survey 2024), with a 10% reef-attributable share applied based on established ecological-economic benchmarks (Spalding et al. 2017). This covers 30 of 40 monitoring units across 4 marine parks.
